Source: the --grab-delay-ms argument of the CI-only probe scripts/ci/xres-owner.c, parsed by strtol and refused only when negative, out of long range or followed by text (scripts/ci/xres-owner.c:864-867); there is no upper bound. Sink: the signed addition delay_ms + 999 in the alarm bound (scripts/ci/xres-owner.c:922). Above LONG_MAX-999 it overflows (undefined behaviour); a value such as 4294967291000 wraps the unsigned cast to alarm(0) and cancels the bound. Not exploitable as shipped: the workflows pass only --mode wm --owner-pid (.github/workflows/release.yml:614) so delay_ms is 0 and the bound is 5 s; anyone able to add the flag already controls the workflow; scripts/ is not published. Verdict hardening: refuse delay_ms above a small ceiling (e.g. 60000) in the same check. Not required before publication.
